{"lyrics":"[Intro]\n[00:00.84]Maybe it wasn't meant to be\n[00:12.04]Maybe it wasn't meant\n[00:15.42]Goose with another one\n[Chorus]\n[00:16.34]Maybe it wasn't meant to be\n[00:19.00]Maybe the drugs will set me free\n[00:24.12]Maybe I ain't mean nothing to her\n[00:29.76]But she meant everything to me, yeah, yeah\n[Verse 1]\n[00:35.64]You better leave her while you got the chance\n[00:38.84]Don't even stay for another dance\n[00:41.66]She got a couple other men\n[00:43.64]It was all part of her plan\n[00:48.24]She knows I'll leave her some day\n[00:54.28]She knows that it's not Sunday\n[00:59.58]So I'm not savin' no ho\n[01:02.14]I don't feel you, we don't feel you\n[01:07.90]Love is unfamiliar, love is unfamiliar\n[Chorus]\n[01:13.24]Maybe it wasn't meant to be\n[01:18.44]Maybe the drugs will set me free\n[01:24.48]Maybe I ain't mean nothing to her\n[01:30.14]But she meant everything to me, yeah, yeah\n[Verse 2]\n[01:36.00]Raf Simons got me feelin' myself\n[01:37.32]Percocet, it got me killin' myself\n[01:41.86]But I still feel like the man\n[01:44.90]Yeah, I still feel like the man with the bands\n[01:47.90]Yeah, I still feel like the man with the plan\n[01:51.32]I thank God for that, I go hard for that\n[01:54.30]For that money, I pulled your card for that\n[01:57.30]For that cash, play your part for that, part in that\n[02:00.58]I gave it my all, you could have it all\n[02:04.50]Gone and God, they sharing me 'cause I'm famous and all\n[02:07.10].40 on my hip I get to aimin' and all\n[02:10.52]Fame and I'm running roof I'm takin' it all\n[Chorus]\n[02:13.60]Maybe it wasn't meant to be\n[02:18.82]Maybe the drugs will set me free\n[02:24.86]Maybe I ain't mean nothing to her\n[02:30.52]But she meant everything to me\n[Verse 3]\n[02:35.06]Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah\n[02:38.68]I'm used to being alone (Yeah, yeah)\n[02:41.68]I don't wanna do it anymore (Yeah)\n[02:44.50]Really hate being alone, more than I hated it before\n[02:50.54]Gotten used to being alone\n[02: